# Forge's route search orders the quests of this guide and its guide writer writes the steps.
# Fixes go into data/route-fixes.json, data/guide-fixes.json or forever-db/corrections, never
# into this file.
# Added here: A Free Lunch (129), Blackrock Blockade (98387); on Duskwood's first loop Raven Hill (163)
# and Jitters' Growling Gut (5), with Jitters on the Raven Hill stop and Chef Grual on the way back.

# Duskwood and Redridge, first half (about 23 to 25.6). Since 2026-11-07
# Duskwood and Redridge are played together, so Redridge comes at 23+ where
# its quests fit (Ashenvale and Stonetalon come first): Duskwood's first loop,
# then Redridge (this guide, with its elites and Fangore on the same loop),
# then Duskwood's second loop (05-duskwood). It comes after Ashenvale,
# Stonetalon and the Wetlands (06-ashenvale, 20-23): the tram from Ironforge
# brings you to Stormwind at about 23.
#
# Flow: Stormwind (training) -> Elwynn road (Theocritus) -> Three Corners ->
# south to Darkshire (flight path, hearth, every quest giver) -> Duskwood's
# first loop (the Duskwood notes are in 05-duskwood) -> Darkshire -> north to Three
# Corners -> Lakeridge Highway (Guard Howe) -> the murlocs east of the
# bridge -> Lakeshire (Baren, hearth, every quest giver) -> Bellygrub's pen
# and Martie -> Lakeshire (the Wanted posters) -> Alther's Mill, the Blackrock
# camps and Gar'im's cave ->
# north through Galardell Valley (Fangore), the Old Lion Statue, the watch
# tower and Stonewatch Keep -> back west along the lake to Render's Valley and
# Keeshan -> Lakeshire with him (every hand-in, one pass north to south), then
# the flight to Darkshire (05-duskwood).
#
# The Battleworn Axes (20) come from the Blackrock camps at the south end of
# Galardell Valley, east of Stonewatch Keep (about 66-74, 63-86): some 40
# Renegade, Grunt and Outrunner spawns, against about ten east of Alther's
# Mill, which Tazul found too few and too slow to respawn (#340). The keep's
# Sentries and Shadowcasters are elite: the camps lie east of them.
#
# Deviations from the export:
# - Since Duskwood's first loop comes first (2026-11-07), Redridge is entered
#   at about 24.5: Galardell Valley's Shadowhide gnolls (median 24) are within
#   two levels, so Solomon's Law (91), A Watchful Eye (94) and Looking Further
#   (248) are taken on the way back west, Bellygrub (34, 24) with Martie's
#   first visit, and Lieutenant Fangore (180, 26) at the valley's north end,
#   with no top-up (#1052's top-up to 23 at the Blackrock camps is gone).
# - Alther's Mill (98386, Forever) is offered by Foreman Oslow only once The
#   Everstill Bridge (89) is handed in (two players' reports; the quest data
#   has no prerequisite for it, #51). Since 2026-11-07 that is at 20, on
#   Redridge's first visit (03-loch-modan), where Oslow gives it with the
#   hand-in; Marshal Marris's Blackrock Menace and Blockade (20, 98387) and
#   Murloc Poachers (150) are taken on that visit too, at their givers, and
#   done here, where level 20-21 quests still give full XP. The tarantulas are
#   still killed on the trip east.
# - Redridge's 15-20 quests (Guard Parker's and Deputy Feldon's gnolls, The
#   Lost Tools and The Everstill Bridge, Darcy's and Martie's errands,
#   Redridge Goulash, Verner's and Solomon's chains, Hilary's Necklace) and the
#   Defias chain from Wiley the Black are done at 19-20 in 03-loch-modan,
#   where they give full XP.
# - The Lakeshire flight path and hearth (listed at the end of Darkshore in
#   the export) are taken on arrival. The Darkshire flight path and hearth
#   the export lists at the end of this visit belong to the Duskwood guide.
# - Left out, accepted but never turned in on the route: Theocritus'
#   Retrieval (178, a pendant drop for the Tower of Azora).
# - Refresh (2026): Expanding Horizons (97914, from 03-darkshore) is handed
#   to Baros Alexston at the Stormwind stop (the end of 06-ashenvale since 2026-11-07: the Cathedral Square, one pass through the city); his reply, Making Do (97926),
#   goes back to Auberdine on 06-wetlands' boat trip to Ashenvale. Baros offers Making Do only
#   after Expanding Horizons (#453), which a player who skipped it in
#   Darkshore does not have, and the project data lists no prerequisite:
#   the accept is optional, so nobody is held at Baros.
# - Lakeshire on arrival: Oslow, Marris, Conacher, the docks (Baren, Wiley),
#   then Breanna and Martie at the west end, one sweep instead of crossing
#   town twice.
#
# Class quests at the Stormwind stop (about level 23, at the end of 06-ashenvale since 2026-11-07): Rogues take Mathias and
# the Defias (2360, Poisons; finished at the end of 05-duskwood), Warlocks
# Devourer of Souls (1716, the Succubus; carried to Takar the Seer in
# 07-thousand-needles), Priests their level 20 spell: Arcane Feedback (5676,
# Human, here), Chastise (5645, Dwarf) and Contingency Plan (94819,
# Gnome) for Ironforge in 06-wetlands, Elune's Grace (5673, Night Elf) for
# Darnassus at the start of 06-wetlands. Night Elf Druids fetch
# the Westfall half pendant for Trial of the Sea Lion (272). Train in
# Stormwind on the way; Shamans take the Deeprun Tram to Ironforge for theirs.
# Paladins: Human Paladins use the Symbol of Life on Henze Faulk by Stone
# Cairn Lake on the road east through Elwynn (The Tome of Divinity, 1786 and
# 1787, from the Stormwind stop of 02-westfall; Redemption at the Stormwind
# stop of 05-duskwood). At 20 Duthorian Rall (Human) or Tiza Battleforge
# (Dwarf) starts The Tome of Valor (1793/1794), the way to Verigan's Fist:
# three dungeons and an escort, the Class guide
# forever/class/paladin/verigans-fist.
#
# Wanted: Gath'Ilzogg and WANTED: Incinerator Gar'im (169, 95999: elites,
# optional with a tip to group up) are on the loop through the Blackrock camps
# and Stonewatch Keep at about 25. Not taken: Tharil'zun and Shadow Magic (19,
# 115: Marshal Marris offers them only once Blackrock Menace and Blackrock
# Blockade, 20 and 98387, are handed in, after the keep), Morganth (249), the
# Speaking of Fortitude and Theocritus' Retrieval chains (343+, 178). Howling in
# the Hills (126, after A Baying of Gnolls in 03-loch-modan): not taken.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Stormwind and the road

step Stormwind
  zone Stormwind City
  tip Train, then leave by the main gate and follow the road east through Elwynn Forest.
  train class only Warrior,Paladin,Hunter,Rogue,Priest,Mage,Warlock,Druid -- Level 18 and 20 spells
  vendor nearest optional

step Woo Ping
  only Warrior
  zone Stormwind City
  when level>=20
  when money>=1g
  when !skill "Polearms" 1
  tip While you're here: learn Polearms from Woo Ping (Trade District, 1 gold); two-handers level a Warrior fastest.
  train 11867                         -- Woo Ping

step Woo Ping
  only Hunter
  zone Stormwind City
  when level>=20
  when money>=1g
  when !skill "Polearms" 1
  tip While you're here: learn Polearms from Woo Ping (Trade District, 1 gold); a Hunter's melee weapon is mostly its stats, and two-handers carry the most.
  train 11867                         -- Woo Ping

step Tram to Ironforge
  only Shaman
  zone Stormwind City
  goto 64.5,7.5 "Tram to Ironforge"

step Shaman training
  only Shaman
  zone Ironforge
  tip Stormwind has no shaman trainer: take the Deeprun Tram from the Dwarven District to Ironforge, train with Eldrun Stormbreaker, then ride the tram back.
  train class

step Fly to Sentinel Hill
  only NightElf,Druid
  zone Stormwind City
  goto 66.3,62.7 "Stormwind flight master"
  fly "Sentinel Hill"

step Half Pendant of Aquatic Endurance
  only NightElf,Druid
  zone Westfall
  tip Fly to Sentinel Hill and head north-west to the coast: the Strange Lockbox lies on the sea floor off the shore. Then head east along the road through Elwynn.
  collect 15882 x1                            -- Half Pendant of Aquatic Endurance: the Strange Lockbox

step Back to Elwynn Forest
  only Shaman
  zone Elwynn Forest
  goto 65.2,69.7 "Elwynn Forest"

step Elwynn Forest
  zone Elwynn Forest
  goto 65.2,69.7 "Elwynn Forest"

step Theocritus
  accept 94                           -- On the top floor

step Henze Faulk
  only Human,Paladin
  zone Elwynn Forest
  tip On the road east, past the Tower of Azora, head north from the bridge to Stone Cairn Lake. Henze Faulk lies south of the lake: use the Symbol of Life on him. The Defias Rogue Wizards around him carry the Defias Script.
  use 6866 quest 1786.1 @72.6,51.41 map 1429 era only Human -- Use the Symbol of Life on Henze Faulk
  turnin 1786 only Human -- Henze Faulk
  accept 1787 only Human
  collect 6846 quest 1787.1 only Human -- Defias Script: Defias Rogue Wizards

step Three Corners
  zone Redridge Mountains
  tip The road east through Elwynn crosses into Redridge at Three Corners, where the roads to Redridge, Duskwood and Elwynn meet: south to Duskwood first.
  goto 15.3,71.5 "Three Corners"

step Duskwood
  zone Duskwood
  goto 75.8,45.3 "Duskwood"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Darkshire

step Darkshire
  tip Follow the road south from Three Corners into Duskwood; Darkshire lies on the east side of the forest.
  tip No Bronze Tube for Look to the Stars? Herble Baubbletump sells it in the house beside Viktori, in limited stock; Neal Allen in Menethil Harbor sells it too.
  getfp "Darkshire" npc 2409              -- Felicia Maline, at the north end of town
  accept 101                              -- Madame Eva, in her house by the tavern; inside
  accept 66                               -- Madame Eva, inside
  sethome "Darkshire" npc 6790            -- Innkeeper Trelayne, Scarlet Raven Tavern
  turnin 66                               -- Clerk Daltry, in the town hall
  accept 56                               -- Commander Althea Ebonlocke, in the town hall
  accept 96139                            -- Sirra Von'Indi, in the house behind the town hall
  accept 164                              -- Elaine Carevin, at the south end of town; inside
  accept 165
  accept 163                              -- Elaine Carevin: Jitters, at Raven Hill
  tip Viktori's house stands at the east end of town. Herble Baubbletump sells engineering goods in the house beside it.
  buy 4371 x1 npc 3133 optional           -- Bronze Tube, from Herble Baubbletump, if you have none
  accept 174                              -- Viktori Prism'Antras, inside
  turnin 174
  accept 175                              -- For Blind Mary, on the hill south-east of town

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Tranquil Gardens

step Tranquil Gardens Cemetery: kill these as you meet them
  zone Duskwood
  tip Skeletal Warriors and Skeletal Mages walk among the graves south-east of Darkshire, below Blind Mary's house on the hill. Every skeleton in Duskwood can drop a Skeleton Finger.
  tip Careful: Because the skeletons stand near each other, running straight in tends to pull several at once.
  collect 2378 quest 101                  -- Skeleton Finger
  kill 203 quest 56                       -- Skeletal Mage
  kill 48 quest 56                        -- Skeletal Warrior

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- West

step Watcher Dodds
  tip Watcher Dodds stands south of the road, at the Yorgen Farmstead.
  accept 245

step Raven Hill
  tip Continue west to Raven Hill. The Memory of Valor glows by the ruined house south of the road; Jitters hides in the house at the west end of the village.
  collect 281046 quest 96139              -- Raven Hill Tome, from the Memory of Valor
  turnin 163                              -- Jitters
  accept 5                                -- for Chef Grual in Darkshire

step Sven's Camp
  tip Follow the road north-west past the cemetery to Sven's camp on the far west edge of the forest. Lars stands beside Sven.
  turnin 164                              -- Sven Yorgen
  accept 95
  accept 226                              -- Lars

step The Hushed Bank: kill these as you meet them
  zone Duskwood
  tip Rabid Dire Wolves roam the woods around the cemetery and Abercrombie, Starving Dire Wolves the hills north-east of him. Pygmy Venom Web Spiders crawl east of the cemetery and drop the venom. Every ghoul of the cemetery's northern half can drop a fang.
  tip Careful: Wolves and other spider types share the area along the Westfall border, so you can easily pull several mobs at once.
  kill 565 quest 226                      -- Rabid Dire Wolf
  kill 213 quest 226                      -- Starving Dire Wolf
  kill 539 quest 245                      -- Pygmy Venom Web Spider
  collect 1130 quest 101                  -- Vial of Spider Venom: Pygmy Venom Web Spiders, Venom Web Spiders and Green Recluses

step Abercrombie
  tip The hermit's shack stands in the woods north-east of the Raven Hill Cemetery.
  turnin 165
  accept 148

step Raven Hill Cemetery: kill these as you meet them
  zone Duskwood
  tip The cemetery lies north of the village. Skeletal Horrors and Skeletal Fiends walk its southern half. Mor'Ladim, an elite, wanders the graves: keep away from him.
  collect 1129 quest 101                  -- Ghoul Fang
  collect 2378 quest 101                  -- Skeleton Finger

